KG42.register("clusters-116f2af7d4ec71909117b5e8",{"id":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v142-d-K006","paper":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility","label":"Full-horizon spatiotemporal clearing and participant response under the computing-capacity-adjusted price","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K006","label":"Full-horizon spatiotemporal clearing and participant response under the computing-capacity-adjusted price","market_meaning":"Demand and supply are declared over time; clearing selects the full-horizon quotas under spatiotemporal nodal balance, network, and computing-resource conditions. The fixed clearing dual prices support participant profit response. DaCe demand uses the computing-capacity-adjusted price, and the zero-adjustment and negative-adjustment branches are retained according to the source conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M06"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"All four chains point to the general spatiotemporal (3.32) model. Demand response belongs to the economic interpretation under fixed duals, and no rebidding or price-iteration procedure is given; the lower-bound dual signs, the directional flow domain, and the transmission-subproblem set remain unclosed.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Hourly quoted prices enter the full-horizon decision, and the nodal and computing-capacity duals then enter the participant response, with an explicit quantity and decision dependence. The specific payment accounts are checked separately by the settlement cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R019","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the demand quoted price and the demand profit and conditional branches under the adjusted price."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R020","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Retains the fact of the hourly supply declaration and does not restore the rejected mathematical object."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R021","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Gives the full-horizon welfare objective and the network, computing, and capacity conditions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R022","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Gives the participant profit decomposition under fixed duals and the clearing-price support."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K006-J01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R019","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R021","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-alpha-d","v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-bar-d","v141-c-R019::x::v141-c-R019-x001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-alpha-d","v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-dbar","v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-d"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same temporal demand quoted price, upper bound, and quota are used in the declaration response and in centralized clearing."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K006-J02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R020","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R021","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C002","v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C004","v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-alpha-p","v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-pbar"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g02-e043"],"rationale":"The source treats the hourly supply declaration as the welfare-cost and capacity input; R020 lacks a parameter object, so only a functional interface is established."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K006-J03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R021","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R022","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C005","v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X001","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X002","v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g04-e25"],"rationale":"The nodal and computing-capacity constraints produce the corresponding duals, which the source uses for the fixed-price profit decomposition; the undefined subproblem set is not filled in on that basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K006-J04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R022","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R019","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X001","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X002","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-pi","v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-omega","v141-c-R019::x::v141-c-R019-x001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E24"],"rationale":"The quantities selected under the dual serve as fixed signals in the demand subproblem, and the demand quota at the same time admits a profit-response interpretation; no new iteration edge is formed."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R021::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R021::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g03-E24"],"rationale":"The same spatiotemporal demand function appears in the quoted-price chain and the price-response chain, and the respective conditions are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R020::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R021::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R021::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g02-e043"],"rationale":"An exhibiting citation of the same hourly supply-declaration function."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R022::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R021::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g04-e25"],"rationale":"Both chains cite the full-horizon clearing function of (3.32)."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R022::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R022::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E24"],"rationale":"The same spatiotemporal price-coordination function; the conditional branches and the dual roles remain independent."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::x::v141-c-R019-x001","v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-d","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same consumer temporal quota lies respectively in centralized clearing and in fixed-price selection; the original unit fields are not changed."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-alpha-d","v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-alpha-d","v141-c-R022::theta::v141-c-R022-T003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"Different local input objects of the same hourly demand quoted price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-bar-d","v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-dbar","v141-c-R022::theta::v141-c-R022-T004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E12"],"rationale":"The same requested capacity limits the spatiotemporal demand quota."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-p","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same spatiotemporal supply quota is used in clearing and in the supplier subproblem."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-alpha-p","v141-c-R022::theta::v141-c-R022-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E11"],"rationale":"The same hourly supply quoted price enters the welfare cost and the supplier profit."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-pbar","v141-c-R022::theta::v141-c-R022-T002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same supply capacity is used for clearing and for the fixed-price subproblem."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O11","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-f","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X007"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same spatiotemporal directional transmission flow; the difference between the real domain and the undefined hourly feasible set continues to be retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O12","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-theta","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same spatiotemporal phase angle is used for clearing and for the transmission subproblem; the hourly set definition is not inferred from this."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O13","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-delta","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same virtual-link quota appears in centralized clearing and in profit selection."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O14","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-alpha-delta","v141-c-R022::theta::v141-c-R022-T005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"The same virtual-link cost quoted price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O15","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-deltabar","v141-c-R022::theta::v141-c-R022-T006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g03-E17"],"rationale":"The same virtual link capacity is used in two decision descriptions."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O16","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-alpha-f","v141-c-R022::theta::v141-c-R022-T007"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E15"],"rationale":"The same hourly directed transmission service offer."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O17","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X001","v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-pi"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E24"],"rationale":"The nodal balance dual is a choice quantity in the outer layer and is fixed as a signal in demand response; the roles of variables and parameters are not rewritten."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K006-O18","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X002","v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-omega"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E24"],"rationale":"The same net computing-capacity dual serves respectively as an outer-layer quantity and a fixed demand signal; the lower-bound sign conflict remains unresolved."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R021 records directed flows as real numbers; the frozen feasible region does not separately list non-negativity constraints for flows, and the DC relationship constrains only the difference between the two directional flows. When solving directly over this domain, a common directed component may leave an objective with positive service cost unbounded below; the flow set left undefined in R022 cannot automatically repair this gap.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-f","v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C005","v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C006","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g03-E17"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B verifies the directed-flow domain actually inherited by M06, and C records it explicitly; non-negativity constraints must not be silently added from M01."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The hourly phase angles and flow feasible set used by R022 are not defined in the supplied text, and it cannot yet be confirmed that they are fully consistent with the hourly cross-sections of the full-time-domain network feasible region in R021.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C006","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X006","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X007","v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E17"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Further verify the definition of the hourly feasible set and its correspondence to the DC relationship, phase-angle bounds, and flow domain, then clarify the mathematical closure of the subproblem."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The source declares the lower-bound computing-capacity dual to be non-negative but writes it as negative in the negative-adjustment branch; the two cannot both hold literally together with the net dual definition. Existing R019 and R022 retain this conflict as is.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-omega-l","v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C002","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently verify the sign convention for the lower-bound dual and the negative-adjustment branch; C will revise it explicitly later; D does not presume a sign correction."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R019-C001 infers from a net adjustment of zero that both the upper and lower duals are zero; this requires the additional premise, given in E24, that the product of the two duals is zero. A net difference of zero alone cannot yield this conclusion, and the applicability in the degenerate-capacity case is also not explained.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R021"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C001","v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C005","v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-dmax"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E24","v141-b-g02-e043"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the complementarity and capacity conditions on which this branch depends; a net adjustment of zero must not be generally interpreted as both duals being zero."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G05","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The source's expansion of (3.34) contains a constant term consisting of the upper-bound dual multiplied by the computing capacity, while the profit-sum shorthand on the last line does not list this term. Although this term does not change participant choices under fixed duals, it varies with the outer-layer duals; existing R022 does not fully define L to confirm the closure of the outer-layer objective.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R021::theta::v141-c-R021-param-dmax","v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B verifies whether the Lagrangian formulation and the shorthand omit price-related constants, and C clarifies the complete dual objective; the current expression is retained without repair."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G06","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The C.2 candidate of R020 was not adopted, and the existing chain has no supply price and capacity parameter objects; the complete inputs of R021 and R022 cannot be regarded as having backfilled that chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R020","v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, revise the mathematical objects and bindings of the bidding chain explicitly according to the C contract, addressing the original C2_nonmathematical_has_math issue."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G07","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R019 gives energy and price units, whereas the cited general spatiotemporal source does not specify these units, and R021 and R022 also retain unit gaps. The same-quantity mapping neither verifies nor fills in the units of measurement.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R019::x::v141-c-R019-x001","v141-c-R019::theta::v141-c-R019-theta-pi","v141-c-R022::x::v141-c-R022-X001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the measurement conventions of the general model; do not automatically substitute case units for the general definition."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G08","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The virtual link and computing-capacity constraints still lack approved independent nodes; this cluster uses only the existing clearing and price functions to carry the internal objects.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R021::x::v141-c-R021-x-delta","v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C006","v141-c-R022::V::coordination.price_signal"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e041","v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g03-E24"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-p-virtual-link","v141-b-g03-P2-computing-capacity-constraint"],"required_work":"Manually review the relevant proposals and direction definitions; do not add nodes, edges, or unapproved identity relations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K006-G09","category":"unverified_source","description":"The clearing formulation, dual decomposition, theorem statement, and conditional branches all come from evidence that remains unverified; the experiment did not conduct an independent source audit.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020","v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g02-e042","v141-b-g02-e043","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E24","v141-b-g04-e25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently verify indices, signs, domains, and dual derivations; the candidate assembly does not mean that the equilibrium conclusion has been scientifically accepted."}]},"rule_refs":["42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R019","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R020","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R021","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R022"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-c0b1423827b26c77","COMP-ee9696b9d6fa489d","KG40-c62513665ebf8550","KG40-ea70ad747d712a0c"]});
